, the moment of inertia about a line $1\\,\\textrm{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =5+{1}^{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045417 true] [17592186128975 1074 "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}4\\text{i} & 3-\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2-2\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 3\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{2-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2\\text{i}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 1-2\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & -3\\text{i} & -2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b_{11} + b_{23} = (-4\\textrm{i}) + (1-2\\textrm{i}) = 1-6\\textrm{i}.$" 13194139535471 17592186045443 true] [17592186129033 1074 "Recall that for any $2 \\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PCP^{-1},$ where \n\n![](images/4a/4a53548a17d9b4fd870ce70285bfc2c57cf6c8d352f75149e5aa7511ef4af853.png)\n\nand $\\mathbf{v}$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda.$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n![](images/aa/aa5738b600440bf8327670fc21cd8005c660def232119b2b4808237d988367bd.png)\n\nwhile\n\n![](images/fc/fc91fcabd47720075061e670f62be9ea9b636070a05cba70752bb7060608b764.png)\n\nSo, our rotation-scaling matrix $C$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\overline{\\lambda}=2-4\\textrm{i},$ \n the complex conjugate of $\\lambda.$ Hence, to construct the matrix $P,$ we use the eigenvector $\\overline{\\mathbf{v}},$ the complex conjugate of $\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nNext, we find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{v} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\text{i} \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v})}+\\text{i}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v}) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v}) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536958 17592186576411 true] [17592186129541 1074 "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =5, & \\,{m}_{3} & =7, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.5, & \\,{x}_{2} & =5, & \\,{x}_{3} & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+5+7 \\\\  & =14\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1.5+5\\cdot 5+7\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =3+25+70 \\\\  & =98\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{98}{14}=7.\n$$" 13194139534177 17592186045417 true] [17592186129542 1074 "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by 