e residual is $5.$" 13194139535995 17592186045417 true] [17592186175889 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =0.5x+7 \\\\  & =0.5(6)+7 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535995 17592186045417 true] [17592186176176 1074 "First, we let $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+20x-8.$ \n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and ${x}_{1}=2-2\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}_{1}}=\\overset{―}{2-2\\text{i}}=2+2\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, \n$(x-(2-2\\text{i}))(x-(2+2\\text{i}))$\nis a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(2-2\\text{i}))(x-(2+2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-(2-2\\text{i}+2+2\\text{i})x+(2-2\\text{i})(2+2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+({2}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+8 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}-4x+8$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-1 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-4x+8\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+20x-8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+16x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+4x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}+4x-8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}-4x+8)(2x-1).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-1=0\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=\\fra