olving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 39 & =30+9{d}^{2} \\\\ 9{d}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =1 \\\\ d & =1\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533453 17592186045417 true] [17592186372286 1074 "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(\\frac{2}{3},2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}+{(y-2)}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}+{(y-2)}^{2})xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}x{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}y+x{y}^{3}-4x{y}^{2}+4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}x{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}-\\frac{4}{3}x{y}^{3}+2x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{9}{2}x{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}+\\frac{81}{4}x-36x+18x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{9}{2}x{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}+\\frac{9}{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+\\frac{17}