{y}_{j} & =8(2-0)(3-2)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 16-4-5\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 7\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=7.\n$$" 13194139535935 17592186045417 true] [17592186545800 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4},$ where $\\theta =m∠C.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ adjacent to $∠C.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AB}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{AB}{8} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\ AB & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535941 17592186045417 true] [17592186545812 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3) & =3\\cdot 2x \\\\ 3x+3\\sqrt{3} & =6x \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & =3x \\\\ x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x=2\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3=\\sqrt{3}\\,(\\sqrt{3})+3=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot BC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$